# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A2-b rev4b canonical-diff gate authority (Requirement: 15 negative bases)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each negative vector is exactly ONE mutation away from an un-mutated, positive-
# shaped baseline fixture. D3S4_NEGATIVE_BASE anchors the positive coverage
# reference (check verifies it exists and is positive). D3S4_NEGATIVE_MUTATION is
# the single allowed mutation kind applied to the stored rows/faults relative to
# the baseline rows rebuilt from the un-mutated fixture:
#   "row_field"  — one field of one stored row differs (metadata id marker)
#   "row_remove" — one stored row removed (N08 header row → feed exact_get ABSENT)
#   "row_add"    — one extra D1-illegal row appended (d1_mutation negatives)
#   "fault_add"  — one Port fault added (fault-script negatives N09/N15)
# check recomputes the baseline rows from the un-mutated fixture (negative salt)
# and requires rows+faults canonical diff == 1 (0 or >=2 ⇒ RED).
